issue_comments.body:
I propose to revert these changes, since they cause Out of Memory on the main branch when running `test_free_threading.test_pickle`. Because of that, the GitHub Action CI jobs fail with exit code 143 (issue gh-150114).

I don't think that this change is correct: **sometimes** (race condition), `test_pickle_dumps_with_concurrent_dict_mutation()` of `test_free_threading.test_pickle` enters an unlimited loop and exhaust the system memory. See the issue gh-150257.

The following code was added to `_pickle` to fix the crash gh-146452:

```
/* gh-146452: Wrap the dict iteration in a critical section to prevent
   concurrent mutation from invalidating PyDict_Next() iteration state. */
static int
batch_dict_exact(PickleState *state, PicklerObject *self, PyObject *obj)
{
    int ret;
    Py_BEGIN_CRITICAL_SECTION(obj);
    ret = batch_dict_exact_impl(state, self, obj);
    Py_END_CRITICAL_SECTION();
    return ret;
}
```

This PR replaces this function with "fine-grained sections".

Problem: `Py_BEGIN_CRITICAL_SECTION(obj);` and `Py_END_CRITICAL_SECTION();` is put around a single `PyDict_Next()` call, whereas [the `PyDict_Next()` documentation](https://docs.python.org/dev/c-api/dict.html#c.PyDict_Next) recommends putting the whole loop in the critical section.

By the way, the 3.15 backport of this PR is different since there was not `batch_dict_exact_impl()` function. Maybe a 3.15 backport of the previous fix was missed?
